  "title": "U.S. Inbound Investment and Industrial-Capex Funding Map 2025–2026",
  "question": "When the administration says trillions of dollars are coming into or being invested in the United States, which legal and economic objects are included and who supplies the cash and carries the credit risk for real industrial projects?",
  "bluf": "The headline aggregate is not a disclosed trillion-dollar construction-debt pipeline. It combines multi-year corporate spending plans, foreign-government investment frameworks, procurement and trade figures, domestic allocations and some named projects; announcement, financing commitment, draw, construction spend and commercial operation remain separate states.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-07-31",
  "use_note": "Evidence through July 31 supports decomposition of aggregate claims, project clocks and six traced financing cases. It does not prove the headline is a disclosed construction-debt pipeline, permit addition across claim families or make six-case risk allocation universal. The separately maintained AI-capital and digital-rail children retain their own questions and cutoffs.",
